cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. All outputs are SYNTHETIC; this is an offline performance-art prototype, not a medical device."
title: "Signal Loom: offline synthetic EEG/ECG-like living score for performance art"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/signal-loom"
url: "https://sparkainlp-x.github.io/signal-loom/"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
version: "0.1.0"
abstract: >-
  Offline browser performance-art prototype by Spark AI NLP. Separate
  synthetic EEG-like and synthetic ECG-like streams become an interactive
  visual score: EEG slow-envelope expands a 2D field, ECG-derived synthetic
  R–R intervals set pulse rhythm, and an adjustable β/τ injection draws a
  timing thread. Includes held-out robustness and shuffled-code mapping
  controls under Node tests. No live sensors, no network requests, no
  medical claims. SYNTHETIC evidence only. Not a medical device, not
  diagnostic, not a physical hologram, not mind reading.
keywords:
  - synthetic
  - EEG-like
  - ECG-like
  - performance-art
  - offline
  - visualization
  - living score
  - research prototype
